  "job_B1.3.34_20251001_193218": {
    "text": "XII KALENDAS IALNUARIAS: PASSIO SANCTI THOME APOSTOLI.\n\u00c6fter \u00fe\u00e6s h\u00e6lendes \u00ferowunge and \u00e6riste of dea\u00f0e and upstige to heofonum, \u00fea \u00fea his apostolas\n\u00dea andwyrde Thomas, Eala \u00feu, min Drihten, send me \u00feyder \u00fee \u00feu wille buton to \u00feam Indiscum.\nSe h\u00e6lend him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Far nu, and ic beo mid \u00fee, and \u00fee ne forl\u00e6te, and \u00e6fter \u00fean \u00fee \u00feu me gestrynst\nThomas him andwyrde, \u00feu eart min Drihten, and ic eom \u00fein \u00feeowa; gewur\u00f0e \u00fein willa.\nEfne \u00fea se gerefa reow him to lande, Abbanes gehaten, fram \u00feam Indiscan kyninge, and eode geond \u00fea\nCrist him \u00fea eode to, and cw\u00e6\u00f0 openlice, Hw\u00e6t bigst \u00feu iunglincg?\nHe andwyrde and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min hlaford, \u00fe\u00e6ra Indiscra cyning, asende me to \u00feysum earde to axienne\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se H\u00e6lend to \u00feam cnihte sona, Ic h\u00e6bbe \u00e6nne wyrhtan wur\u00f0fulne and getreowne, \u00feone ic oft\n\u00deisne ic wille sendan gif \u00feu swa wylt mid \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu mid wur\u00f0mynte \u00e6fter \u00feam weorce eft hine asende\n\u00dea blissode Abbanes, and beah to his cneowum, and se H\u00e6lend bet\u00e6hte \u00feone halgan Thoman him ham\n\u00dea axode Abbanes \u00feone arwur\u00f0an apostol, Sege me to so\u00fean, gif \u00feu sy his \u00feeowa?\nThomas him andwyrde, Gif ic his \u00e6ht n\u00e6re, ic wolde forseon sona his h\u00e6sa; ac ic eom his \u00feeowa, and\nIc eom an his \u00feeowena of \u00feam ungerimum, and we ealle cunnon cr\u00e6ftas on weorcum, and fara\u00f0 geond\nHi eodon \u00fea to scipe and heora segel ar\u00e6rdon, and mid winde ferdon swa swa him gewissode God.\nAbbanes \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft to \u00feam apostole, Gif \u00feu canst on cr\u00e6ftum swa swa \u00feu cw\u00e6de nu \u00e6r, hwi wolde\nThomas him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to be Cristes getimbrunge, Ic lecge \u00fea grundweallas \u00fee gel\u00e6sta\u00f0 \u00e6fre, and ic sette\nIc ar\u00e6re \u00fea getimbrunge, \u00fe\u00e6t hire hrof oferstih\u00f0 ealle gebytlu, and bi\u00f0 utan f\u00e6ger, and swa\u00feeah wlitigre\nSwa hw\u00e6t swa bi\u00f0 on marmstane, o\u00fe\u00fee on m\u00e6rlicre getimbrunge, ic so\u00felice wyrce; and gif \u00feu wilt me\nAbbanes \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00e6nlic is se wer \u00fee swilce wyrhtan h\u00e6f\u00f0, he is selra \u00feonne sum kynincg.\nThomas him andwyrde, \u00e6nlice \u00feu spr\u00e6ce.\nKyninges sunu he is, ancenned his f\u00e6der, and hylt his f\u00e6der rice on healicum muntum, \u00fe\u00e6r nan feond\nHi seglodon \u00fea for\u00f0 seofon niht on an, and on land eodon; ac hit bi\u00f0 langsum to secganne ealle \u00fea\nHi comon \u00fea \u00e6t nextan to \u00fe\u00e6m cyninge on India, and Abbanes gebrohte ardlice Thoman to \u00fe\u00e6s\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he mihte.\n\u00dea sceawodon hi \u00feone stede \u00fe\u00e6r hit standan sceolde, and Thomas eode metende mid anre metegyrde\n\u00dea beheold se cyning and cw\u00e6\u00fe to \u00feam apostole, \u00feu eart \u00e6\u00feela cr\u00e6fta and kynegum \u00feu sceoldest\nSe cyning \u00fea bet\u00e6hte \u00feam Cristes wyrhtan ungerim feos to for\u00f0igenne \u00fe\u00e6t weorc, and rad geond his\nThomas \u00fea ferde freolice bodigende Godes geleafan geond \u00fe\u00e6t land gehw\u00e6r, and fullode \u00fea\nHit gelamp \u00fea swa \u00fe\u00e6t he to geleafan gebigde ungerim folces and fyr\u00f0rode cyrcan, and preostas\nHit wear\u00f0 \u00fea gecydd \u00feam cyninge \u00feus, and he het gebindan begen mid racenteagum, Abbanes and\n\u00dea l\u00e6g \u00fe\u00e6s cyninges bro\u00f0or his lifes orwene, se w\u00e6s Gad gehaten, Gundofore swi\u00f0e leof, and he\nMid \u00feam \u00fee he wolde hi to w\u00e6fersyne tucian, \u00fea gewat se Gad of worulde to helle.\nMan heold \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t lic on \u00fea h\u00e6\u00f0enan wisan, and se bro\u00f0or wolde wur\u00f0lice hine bestandan, and\n\u00dea on \u00feone feor\u00f0an d\u00e6g f\u00e6rlice on mergen aras se ylce Gad ar\u00e6red \u00feurh God, and \u00fea licmen wurdon\n\u00dea clypode se geedcucode and cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his bre\u00f0er, Gehyr nu min bro\u00f0or be \u00feam halgan men \u00feone \u00f0e\nMin sawl w\u00e6s gel\u00e6d so\u00felice to heofonum \u00feurh Godes englas, and ic \u00fe\u00e6r geseah \u00fea m\u00e6ran gebytlu \u00fee\nMid \u00feam \u00fee ic sceawode \u00fea scinendan gebytlu, \u00fea s\u00e6don me \u00fea englas, \u00feis synd \u00fea gebytla \u00fee\nIc wiscte \u00fea \u00fe\u00e6t ic moste on \u00feam m\u00e6ran huse huru durewerd beon.\nDrihtnes englas \u00fea cw\u00e6don, \u00fein bro\u00f0or nis wyr\u00f0e \u00feises weorces f\u00e6gernysse; gif \u00feu hit habban wylt\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum wordum he efste to \u00feam cwearterne, and gesohte \u00feone apostol secgende mid wope, Min\nHe unband hine sona, and b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he underfenge deorwur\u00f0e gyrlan.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Drihtnes \u00feegen, Git \u00feu nast \u00fe\u00e6t ne weria\u00f0 wuldorfulle gyrlan ne fl\u00e6sclice fr\u00e6tewunga \u00fea \u00fee\n\u00dees pallium \u00fee ic werige wyle me gel\u00e6stan, and min syric ne tosih\u00f0, ne mine sceos ne tob\u00e6rsta\u00f0, \u00e6r\nEfne \u00fea \u00fea hi uteodon of \u00feam ealdan cwearterne, \u00fea gesohte Gundoforus \u00feone Godes apostol,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Thomas him to, Crist min Drihten h\u00e6f\u00f0 micel geti\u00feod \u00feurh his mildheortnysse eow, \u00fe\u00e6t he\nNu syndon eowre scira and eowre ceastra afyllede mid halgum cyrcum, and \u00fe\u00e6s H\u00e6lendes geleafan;\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 sona Gad to \u00feam Godes apostole, \u00fea gebytlu ic sceawode \u00fee \u00feu minum bre\u00feer getimbrodest,\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 bli\u00feelice Thomas, hit stent on \u00feinum bre\u00feer gif \u00feu hit gebicgan most.\nSe cyning \u00fea Gundoforus cw\u00e6\u00f0 to his bre\u00feer, Nu hit me geworht is, ic wene \u00fe\u00e6t hit min beo; wyrce se\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se halga apostol, Se H\u00e6lend h\u00e6f\u00f0 getimbrod ungerime wununge and widgylla gebytlu fram\nGif ge willa\u00f0 nu beon embe \u00fea gebytlu swi\u00f0or, and embe \u00fea heofonlican speda sprecan on eornost,\nL\u00e6ta\u00f0 nu eowre \u00e6hta wydewum fremian, w\u00e6dlum, and wanhalum, and wita\u00f0 to so\u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t hi be\n\u00dea asprang his hlisa geond \u00fe\u00e6t land wide \u00fe\u00e6t to Indian come Cristes apostol, se \u00fee mihte geh\u00e6lan mid\n\u00dea wende \u00fe\u00e6t landfolc \u00fe\u00e6t he w\u00e6re God sylf, and brohton him kynehelmas, and budon him gyrlan\nThomas \u00fea gecw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi comon ealle to anum gemote \u00fe\u00e6t he mihte him secgan hw\u00e6t him to donne\nHi comon \u00fea feorran to anum felde eft, and manega \u00feider feredon mislice untrume, \u00fe\u00e6t se halga\n\u00dea het se halga apostol ahebban \u00fea seocan on anre stowe ealle, and stod him tomiddes upastrehtum\n\u00c6fter \u00feysre clypunge \u00fea hi cw\u00e6don, amen.\n\u00dea com \u00fe\u00e6r swilc leoht, swilce \u00fe\u00e6r liget brude, \u00fe\u00e6t hi ealle wendon \u00fe\u00e6t hi forwur\u00f0an sceoldon, and\n\u00dea aras Thomas up and het hi arisan and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min Drihten sylf com hider swa swa scinende liget,\n\u00dea arison \u00fea wanhalan wundorlice geh\u00e6lede wuldrigende \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan and his arwur\u00fean apostol.\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea Thomas astah to anum stane and stod \u00fe\u00e6t hi ealle mihton hine \u00e6nne geseon, and clypode\nSe H\u00e6lend me asende to \u00feysum earde hider and ic his \u00feeowa eom, mann swa swa ge syndon, and he\nHe t\u00e6hte \u00fea langlice geleafan \u00feam folce, and hu hi leahtres forbugon and bysmorlice d\u00e6da, and hu hi\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft to \u00fe\u00e6re meniu \u00fee on \u00feam gemote w\u00e6ron, Ne eom ic na God, ac eom Godes \u00feeowa;\nHi dydon sona swa, and on \u00feone Sunnand\u00e6g wurdon feowertyne \u00feusenda gefullode on Criste butan\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se halga Thomas gewissod eft \u00feurh God \u00fe\u00e6t he sceolde faran to \u00fe\u00e6re fyrran Indian, and\nHe geh\u00e6lde \u00fe\u00e6r \u00feurh God healte and blinde and ealle untrumnyssa, and \u00fea egeslican hreoflian, and\n\u00de\u00e6t landfolc \u00fea ne mihte his lare wi\u00f0cwe\u00fean, \u00feonne he swilce wundra geworhte him \u00e6tforan.\nSum wif hatte Sintice, seo w\u00e6s six gear blind, and wear\u00f0 \u00fea geh\u00e6led \u00e6t \u00feam halgan apostole, and\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Migdonia, \u00fees man is God sylf o\u00f0\u00f0e Godes engel, \u00fee \u00feine eagan onlihte swa butan\nAnd hi swa lange spr\u00e6con o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t hi eodon butu \u00fe\u00e6r se apostol bodode.\nMigdonia \u00fea gelyfde on \u00feone lifigendan God, \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6s apostoles lare, and leng nolde cuman to hire\nSeo Migdonia w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s kyninges wifes swuster, and hire wer \u00fea gemacode wi\u00f0 Migdeum \u00feone kyning\nMigdonia \u00fea com to \u00feam cwearterne dreorig, and feoll to his fotum mid fyrhte cwe\u00f0ende, Ic bidde \u00fee,\nSe godes man hire cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, Gang \u00fee ham ongean, and ic cume ham to \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu oncnawe \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t,\nHeo dyde \u00fea swa, and hire dura beleac, licgende on gebedum on hire bure astreht.\nEfne \u00fea se apostol on \u00fe\u00e6re ylcan nihte com to Migdonian and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Swa swa \u00feu becymst \u00feurh me to\nBeo nu swi\u00fee anr\u00e6de.\nHeo andwyrde mid fyrhte, La leof, ic \u00fee bidde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu onlihte mine sawla, \u00fe\u00e6t ic geseon mage \u00feone\nThomas hire cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, cep \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu f\u00e6ste seofon dagas georne, and ic sy\u00f0\u00f0an cume eft to \u00fee, and \u00fee\n\u00c6fter \u00feysum com hire wer to \u00feam kyninge Migdeum and b\u00e6d georne \u00feone kyning \u00fe\u00e6t seo cwen\n\u00dea ge\u00feafode se cynincg \u00fe\u00e6t seo cwen \u00feider eode, and heo cw\u00e6\u00f0 sona to hire swuster \u00f0us, Eala \u00feu\nSe kyning sylf hit bem\u00e6n\u00f0, and his men ealle, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu swa f\u00e6rlice forlure \u00fein gewitt.\nMigdonia hire andwyrde, Eala \u00feu, min swuster, wistest \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t ic wat, \u00feas word \u00feu ne cw\u00e6de.\nSe apostol wyrc\u00f0 fela wundra on mannum, and s\u00e6g\u00f0 us to so\u00fean \u00fe\u00e6t sy o\u00feer lif undeadlic and ece,\nNu to niht eode se ealdorman him to, for\u00fean\u00fee his suna w\u00e6s f\u00e6rlice dead, and l\u00e6dde \u00feone apostol to\nNu he sitt, and l\u00e6r\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6r geleafan on \u00feam huse, and geh\u00e6l\u00f0 \u00fea untruman, ealle \u00fee him to cuma\u00f0.\nTriptia seo cwen cw\u00e6\u00f0 hire to andsware, Gif hit swa is, swa \u00feu s\u00e6gst, ic wille geseon \u00feone man.\nDyslic bi\u00f0 to forseonne so\u00f0lice \u00fe\u00e6t ece lif, and heardmod bi\u00f0 se man \u00fee ne mage \u00feysum gelyfan.\nHi eodon \u00fea butu his bodunge to gehyrenne; hi gemetton \u00fea \u00feone apostol micclum gebysgod ofer \u00fea\n\u00dea \u00f0a seo cwen geseah swilce wundra \u00e6t him, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 heo ofwundrod, Awyrgede synd \u00fea men \u00fee\n\u00dea stod \u00fe\u00e6r an hreofla tohrorenum lichaman, atelic on hiwe, and hine geh\u00e6lde Thomas, and hine\nHeo feol \u00fea to his fotum, fulluhtes biddende, and \u00fe\u00e6s ecan lifes mid geleafan gewilnode, and cw\u00e6\u00f0\nThomas \u00fea bletsode bli\u00feelice \u00fea cwene, and l\u00e6rde hi georne to geleafan and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min Drihten me\nHe gefullode hi \u00fea, and fela o\u00fere mid hire wera and wifa, and \u00fea unwittigan cild, and l\u00e6rde hi georne\n\u00dea com seo cwen on \u00e6fnunge to \u00feam cyninge ham, and he cw\u00e6\u00f0 hire sona to, Swy\u00f0e lange \u00feu w\u00e6re.\nHeo cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft him to, Ge cw\u00e6don \u00fe\u00e6t min swuster, and ic sylf eac wende, \u00fe\u00e6t heo gewitleas w\u00e6re; ac\nSo\u00f0lice ic geseah \u00feone sylfan apostol se \u00fee halwende r\u00e6d \u00e6ghwylcum men forgif\u00f0.\nNu \u00feu kyning miht macian \u00fee undeadlicne gif \u00feu wilt gehyran \u00feone halgan apostol; ne swyltst \u00feu on\n\u00dea forhtode se cyning, and het feccan him to \u00feone fores\u00e6dan \u00feegen \u00fee hire swustor h\u00e6fde, and\nAnd hi motodon lange.\n\u00dea het se kyning gebringan on bendum him Thoman, and axode mid graman, Hw\u00e6t is se, eower God,\nThomas him cw\u00e6\u00f0 to, \u00feu kyning wilt habban cl\u00e6nlice \u00feenunga and gecwema \u00feenas; wenst \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Migdeus se kyning, Gemaca mid wordum eft \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea wif gecyrran sylfwilles to us.\nThomas him andwyrde, Ic worhte \u00e6nne stypel, and \u00feu cwy\u00f0st \u00fe\u00e6t ic sceolde sylf hine towurpan; ac ic\nAnd he cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft him to, \u00feu kyning ne miht ofslean \u00fea sawle mid w\u00e6pnum, \u00feeah \u00f0e \u00feu \u00feone lichaman\nGod se so\u00f0f\u00e6sta kyning m\u00e6g asendan \u00e6g\u00f0er ge sawle ge lichaman to \u00feam ecan fyre.\n\u00de\u00e6t wif moste \u00fea swa hire wer forl\u00e6tan for\u00fean\u00fee he h\u00e6\u00feen w\u00e6s, and hetol ehtere; ac canones\n\u00dea het se kyning lecgan hate isena sona under his nacodum fotum, \u00fe\u00e6t he lange swa \u00ferowode, ac \u00fe\u00e6s\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 Thomas him to, Ne dyde God \u00feis for me, ac for \u00fee swi\u00feor, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu swa huru gelyfde on \u00feone\nWitodlice he m\u00e6g \u00fea mihte me syllan \u00fe\u00e6t ic butan w\u00e6tere \u00fein wite me ne ondr\u00e6de.\n\u00dea het Migdeus se kyning \u00feone Godes man gedon on weallende w\u00e6ter; \u00fea wear\u00f0 hit acolod, and nan\nHe wear\u00f0 \u00fea gel\u00e6d to \u00feam lifleasum godum \u00fe\u00e6t he his lac sceolde lecgan him on offrunga, and his\n\u00dea geb\u00e6d hine Thomas bealdlice to his Drihtne, and het \u00feone scuccan \u00fee on \u00feam scincr\u00e6fte wunode\n\u00dea eode se deofol of \u00fe\u00e6re anlicnysse ut, and towende hi sona, swa swa wex formylt, swa \u00fe\u00e6t ne belaf\n\u00dea clypodon \u00fea h\u00e6\u00feengildan, and hetelice grimetodon, and heora an sona ofsloh \u00feone apostol mid\nHi feredon \u00fea his lic mid geleafan to cyrcan, and wur\u00f0lice bebyrigdon, to wuldre \u00feam \u00e6lmihtigan.\n\u00de\u00e6r wurdon gelome wundra gefremode; wode men \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6ron on gewitte gebrohte, and gehwilce",
